---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PublicRecordCard from '../components/PublicRecordCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Macro Evidence | Open Infrastructure for Macroeconomic Evidence."
  description="Macro Evidence builds open macroeconomic data infrastructure around provenance, validation, reproducibility, transparent limitations, and public governance."
>
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="site-container home-hero-inner">
      <div class="home-hero-copy">
        <h1>Open Infrastructure for Macroeconomic Evidence.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          We build open macroeconomic data infrastructure around provenance,
          validation, reproducibility, and transparency. Macro Data Observatory
          (MDO) is our flagship and foundational platform.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="primary-action" href="/software">Explore software</a>
          <a class="secondary-action" href="/about">About us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section premise-section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-lead-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">How we work</span>
          <h2>Evidence is more useful when its path stays visible.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="reading">
          <p class="section-intro">
            We treat provenance, validation, reproducibility, maintainability,
            and transparent limitations as engineering requirements. The goal is
            practical: make the work easier to inspect, reproduce, and improve.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/principles">Read how we work →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-grid mt-3">
        <article class="principle-card">
          <span class="question">Where did it come from?</span>
          <h3>Provenance</h3>
          <p>
            Keep source identity and lineage represented or documented to the
            depth the system actually implements.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <span class="question">What rules did it pass?</span>
          <h3>Validation</h3>
          <p>
            Make checks explicit without turning documented rules into claims of
            broader methodological assurance.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <span class="question">Can it be recreated?</span>
          <h3>Reproducibility</h3>
          <p>
            Document pipelines, configuration, and transformation logic so
            results do not depend on hidden manual judgment.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <span class="question">What are the limits?</span>
          <h3>Transparency</h3>
          <p>
            State relevant methodology, decisions, and material limitations
            plainly instead of letting confidence outrun evidence.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section foundation-section">
    <div class="site-container foundation-grid">
      <div class="foundation-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">Our shared foundation</span>
        <h2>
          Macro Evidence sets the direction. MDO turns it into working
          infrastructure.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Macro Evidence is the organization: mission, stewardship, governance,
          standards, and the broader software direction. Macro Data Observatory
          is the flagship and foundational platform where that direction becomes
          macroeconomic-data infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <article class="platform-feature">
        <span class="micro-label">Flagship and foundational platform</span>
        <h3>Macro Data Observatory</h3>
        <p>
          Open-source data infrastructure for acquiring, validating,
          structuring, and maintaining macroeconomic data from authoritative
          public sources through engineered, reproducible pipelines.
        </p>
        <div class="platform-status">
          <span>Status</span>
          <strong>Under active development.</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a
            class="primary-action"
            href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/macro-data-observatory"
          >
            Open MDO on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section records-section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-lead-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Public record</span>
          <h2>You should not have to take our word for it.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="reading">
          <p class="section-intro">
            Our mission, decision process, documentation standards, and other
            institutional records are public and versioned. The website provides
            the context; the canonical records remain with the public
            repositories on GitHub that own them.
          </p>
          <p class="institutional-line">
            Audit the evidence. Decide what to trust.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="record-grid mt-3">
        <PublicRecordCard
          kicker="Direction"
          title="Organization & Platform Charter"
          description="Our mission, vision, organization/platform scope, and durable direction."
          href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/governance/blob/main/ORGANIZATION_CHARTER.md"
          linkLabel="Read Organization & Platform Charter"
        />
        <PublicRecordCard
          kicker="Decisions"
          title="Governance & Decision-Making Charter"
          description="How consequential organization-wide decisions are evaluated, recorded, and approved."
          href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/governance/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md"
          linkLabel="Read Governance & Decision-Making Charter"
        />
        <PublicRecordCard
          kicker="Standards"
          title="Documentation Standards"
          description="How documentation ownership, writing, naming, versioning, and commit conventions are maintained."
          href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/governance/blob/main/DOCUMENTATION_STANDARDS.md"
          linkLabel="Read Documentation Standards"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section engage-band">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="engage-intro">
        <span class="eyebrow">Take part</span>
        <h2>Build with us. Ask questions. Support the work.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Whether you want to contribute, start a conversation, or help sustain
          the infrastructure, there is a clear place to begin.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="path-grid">
        <article class="path-card">
          <h3>Contribute</h3>
          <p>
            Help improve our software, documentation, and public infrastructure.
          </p>
          <a href="/contribute">Contribute →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="path-card">
          <h3>Contact</h3>
          <p>
            Start a conversation about the work, collaboration, or an
            institutional question.
          </p>
          <a href="/contact">Get in touch →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="path-card">
          <h3>Sponsor</h3>
          <p>
            Help sustain the open infrastructure and ongoing engineering behind
            it.
          </p>
          <a href="/sponsor">Support the work →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
